If you need a visa to enter the UK and need a formal letter to support your visa application to attend the interview; or require any adjustments to support you during the interview process, please let me know as soon as possible.

Next steps:

The research proposal section of your application will be sent to external experts for written review before your interview. The reviews will form part of the information provided to the Interview Committee. We will send you these anonymised comments approximately one week before your interview.

The Early-Career Award Interview Committee consists of a Co-Chair and core members, as outlined on our website (https://wellcome.org/research-funding/guidance/how-wellcome-makes-funding-decisions/funding-application-advisory-committees).

Additional individuals may be invited, on occasion, to join the Committee, however, please note that a bespoke Committee is not assembled for each interview. We will provide you with a list of the individuals who are expected to be present in the interview room approximately one week before the interview. 

Key details about your interview:
Your interview will last for 30 minutes and will consist of a ten-minute Power Point presentation from you followed by twenty minutes of questions from the Committee. Presentations should be widescreen (16:9) format. There is no limit to the number of slides that can be shown, but you will be kept strictly to the time limit.
 
The content of your presentation is up to you, but the Committee may find it useful if you specifically reference the key elements of the assessment criteria for the scheme, which are outlined on the Early-Career Award webpage, which can be found on our website, https://wellcome.org/research-funding/schemes.
 
Within your presentation, you should also address important points raised in the expert reviewers’ comments and provide any updates on developments since the initial submission, if appropriate.
 
In the 20-minute Q&A that follows, you will be expected to answer detailed questions not only on the research proposal but also on your skills and experience and your research environment, including your experience of, and plans for, contributing to a positive and inclusive research culture.
Whilst some questions will be informed by the comments from expert reviewers, members may also ask questions that are not covered in these comments. As there is limited time for questions at the interview, you are advised to keep your answers succinct.
 
You will be assessed on your research proposal (50% of the total score), your own skills and experience (25%) and your research environment (25%).
 
For more information on what to consider when preparing for your interview, please see the following page: https://wellcome.org/research-funding/guidance/prepare-to-apply/how-to-prepare-funding-interview
